       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day. That is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and a single 5 g dose is already above the maximum single dose. At that level it risks severe hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day), which is common for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 5000 mg, please confirm and tell me the clinical reason. I'd still advise against it."
