     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day of acetaminophen. That is well above the toxic threshold of about 150 mg/kg, or roughly 10.5 g for a 70 kg patient, and there is no therapeutic indication for it. It would put the patient at serious risk of acute liver failure. You also haven't given a clinical reason for it.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum). I can enter either one now.\n- **Check for a typo.** If you meant 500 mg or 650 mg, tell me and I'll enter it.\n- **Talk to pharmacy.** If you have an unusual situation in mind, a clinical pharmacist or toxicology can review it with you. Poison control is at 1-800-222-1222 in the US.\n\nIf the patient needs stronger pain or fever control, I can help enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus an NSAID or another agent that suits them."
      }
     ],
